{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"exact-identities-and-reductions","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:769caa5446ebaa913984f2749a14b27d279557c152a9106f683289cc625e0c17/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=8634d96f2643f13a5df640f66e9affa4d4ccfe6fd956bfdc981e788a24eac460","passage_ref":"sha256:f7c2487ba172be55e583becc143742c2d34c576d0d1339fd730197a0c97bb374/papers/long.md/sha256:769caa5446ebaa913984f2749a14b27d279557c152a9106f683289cc625e0c17/papers/long.json/passages/exact-identities-and-reductions","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=8634d96f2643f13a5df640f66e9affa4d4ccfe6fd956bfdc981e788a24eac460&paper=long&passage=exact-identities-and-reductions","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=8634d96f2643f13a5df640f66e9affa4d4ccfe6fd956bfdc981e788a24eac460&paper=long&passage=exact-identities-and-reductions","span":{"end_byte":190836,"end_line":2055,"start_byte":157177,"start_line":1656},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=8634d96f2643f13a5df640f66e9affa4d4ccfe6fd956bfdc981e788a24eac460&view=arguments&node=long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=8634d96f2643f13a5df640f66e9affa4d4ccfe6fd956bfdc981e788a24eac460&node=long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=8634d96f2643f13a5df640f66e9affa4d4ccfe6fd956bfdc981e788a24eac460&node=long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=8634d96f2643f13a5df640f66e9affa4d4ccfe6fd956bfdc981e788a24eac460&view=arguments&node=long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=8634d96f2643f13a5df640f66e9affa4d4ccfe6fd956bfdc981e788a24eac460&ref=sha256%3A57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176%2Fnodes%2Flong.lem-mersenne-tail-weight","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight"],"id":"long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.34 (Each Mersenne weight exceeds its remaining tail)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.34, p. 54, label lem:mersenne-tail-weight","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For $n\\ge1$, let $w_n=(2^n-1)^{-1}$ and $R_n=\\sum_{j>n}w_j$. Then\n$$\nR_n=w_{n+1}+R_{n+1},\\qquad\n 2^{-n}<R_n\\le2w_{n+1}<w_n.\n$$\nFor the upper bound, compare each tail term with $2^{1-j}w_{n+1}$ at index $n+j$, $j\\ge1$, and sum the geometric series. The last inequality follows by comparing $2/(2^{n+1}-1)$ with $1/(2^n-1)$. This strict term-versus-tail inequality is the separation hypothesis used in the greedy arguments.*\n\n*It is not available for the totient weights $\\varphi(n)/2^n$: the terms at indices $4$ and $5$ already sum to $2/16+4/32=1/4=\\varphi(3)/2^3$, and the remaining tail is positive. A general strict-tail argument therefore cannot be transferred to that sequence without a different hypothesis or proof.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.halfTwoChannelCap_lt_mersenneTail%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-mersenne-tail-weight%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.halfTwoChannelCap_lt_mersenneTail%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sh